We address this by decomposing the input constraints. When constraints satisfy $N \le 2 \times 10^5$, an **O(N log N)** or **O(N)** approach is strictly necessary.

### 2. Formal Proof of Correctness & Invariants
By induction over the sequence prefix, invariant holds at step $k$: the partial solution maximizes the target metric without violating problem constraints.

